package com.wjx.touhou_aifun.chat.agent;

/** Stable action guidance belongs in the cacheable policy, not every mutable checkpoint. */
public final class AgentTaskInstructions {
    private AgentTaskInstructions() { }
    /**
     * Required owner-visible narration: the executor must report execution status in its own text,
     * including a factual summary of the latest tool results. Archived for foreground inspection.
     */
    public static final String NARRATION_POLICY = "## Required execution narration\n"
            + "Every response MUST open with a short factual status paragraph in plain text BEFORE any tool call. "
            + "When the previous turn returned tool results, first summarize their actual outcome: what was observed, found, opened, moved, crafted, eaten or delivered; exact counts, item names and positions; and any failure, retry or timeout. "
            + "Use only facts present in the tool results or the checkpoint; never invent, round or claim unverified success. "
            + "Keep it to 1-3 compact sentences. Do not use roleplay, emotion markers, TTS text, tool ids, JSON or a direct owner address. "
            + "The FINAL response must be a factual execution report: what was actually completed or unmet, actual counts and positions, and the blocker if any. "
            + "This narration is archived and may be read by the owner's foreground conversation; it is never spoken, never shown as a chat bubble, and never changes completion verification.\n";
    /** Injected into the next checkpoint when a response dispatched tools without a status line. */
    public static final String NARRATION_REMINDER = "Your previous response dispatched tools without the required status narration. In THIS response, before any tool call, write one short factual status paragraph that also summarizes the tool results above (actual counts, positions and any failure), then continue.";
    public static final String DECISION_HINT = "Native finite decisions are optional. Register the FULL completion contract in the normal plan; runtime can automatically execute observed same-direction multi-container transfer phases from that contract and settled receipts. Other phases use normal tools directly; do not invent a full executable plan or add a planning call solely for native handoff. Only when another reusable/branching segment would save model rounds, load group:task_actions for its syntax. Keep every owner requirement and verified completion condition.\n";
    public static final String DECISION_POLICY="## Typed decision execution\n"
            +"An independent JEV/Decider service evaluates finite choices, not free-text plans. Keep the FULL completion contract, but action_steps may describe only the next useful execution segment. Do not pre-plan unknown future observations. Register an action_steps segment in ONE standalone update_task_plan call; never combine it with duplicate actions. Normal tool calls remain valid. One fixed alternative executes directly; multiple alternatives and omitted enum/boolean parameters use the decision service. Unknown required free-text parameters or visual operations return to you. Never build text by chaining choices.\n"
            +"Startup can bind template, targets, named items and literal quantities in one bounded native request; source menus are still required for unknown amounts and multi-source allocation. When full planning is needed, startup may first select ONE relevant skill from the actual registered catalogue and call use_skill. The loaded guidance is supplied to you for full planning; loading it neither executes its instructions nor proves any owner requirement complete. Native skill choices use actual names and descriptions; do not invent skills or repeatedly reload already supplied guidance. Skill body/reference changes invalidate a pending selection.\n"
            +"The ordinary ordered-batch guidance applies only to plans without action_steps; action_steps must be submitted alone. Use $live.session_id and $live.revision for the currently open GUI. For the Nth atomic completion condition, transfer arguments may bind slot=$live.from_slot_N, to_slot=$live.to_slot_N, count=$live.transfer_count_N; code calculates remaining amounts and legal current slots. Use an until predicate for repeated transfers, so the step stops only when its actual required quantity has been delivered. Use skip_if on opening/preparation steps already made unnecessary by verified completion; until would repeat that preparation instead of advancing. Use $live bindings instead of saving predicted/stale session or slot ids. Fixed targets must come from the owner's scope and fresh observations. Optional target_binding selects only already observed block/container/entity candidates by description and kind, binding $target.x/y/z/registry_id/entity_id/entity_uuid in arguments; never invent coordinates or entity identity.\n"
            +"Startup may select a complete common follow/sit/schedule/work-mode/receive/deliver template, including offered ordered two-component combinations, without an execution LLM call. Explicit per-target quantities can skip reconnaissance; unknown/all source counts and unresolved collective allocation still need inspection. Same-container transfers share one opening; every item and remaining amount is independently verified. An already opened inspection menu can be reused. Optional target_binding.scope identifies ONE subtask: identical scoped queries reuse a previously selected target only while its current identity and labels still match. Use distinct scopes for independent choices, especially after movement. Bindings expire on amendments and new generations. Limited explicit owner amendments can change existing counts, observed targets or existing final states while preserving unaffected requirements and committed facts. Unsupported edits, new jobs, ambiguity or unrepresented quantities return to you for full planning. Work-mode selection does not prove that work was completed. All typed steps and the FULL completion contract must pass server verification before automatic completion. maid_state verifies follow/sit/schedule/work_task; eat_food verifies actual consumed servings and optional finished. Known stale menus or lost sessions may refresh/reopen the same authorized target; ambiguous physical failures select a finite recovery strategy. Recovery is bounded to two attempts per step and always preserves committed facts and remaining quantities. Unsafe one-off mutations, unknown bindings, unsupported failures or uncertainty return to the execution LLM. Do not replay committed facts or weaken the completion contract without an explicit owner amendment.\n";
    public static final String POLICY = "## AIFun action execution rules\n"
            + "Known landmarks are verified absolute block positions, not current observations. Prefer those coordinates; approach within 16 blocks and recheck the target before opening. Identical scans share observation_key/same_observation_as; use the retained detailed copy instead of scanning again only to reread it. Keep the latest required world observation and inspect again when the world, position, target or requested scope changes. Historical geometry never authorizes actions. Checkpoint recent_evidence may reference results already present; durable completed_net_transfers/completed_actions remain authoritative. Owner amendments are ordered in constraints; the last entry supersedes conflicting earlier requirements only.\n"
            + "For cooking, query_recipes includes live smelting/blasting/smoking/campfire routes with ingredients, station and duration. Workbench alternatives do not exclude smelting. Operate the actual station and fuel, and check current stock/receipts before acquiring more ingredients. For an explicit owner return/throw request use drop_items_to_owner with exact remaining item counts; register drop_to_owner completion for every item and close the current GUI first. The action approaches the owner and emits actual entity receipts; inventory=0 alone never proves handoff and successful throwing does not assert pickup. Never emulate dropping via outside clicks or Q. Preserve unrelated items and do not reacquire already held materials. For an unfamiliar mod machine, open its actual GUI and call inspect_gui(visual=true) before moving items. Use the image, nested widget labels/tooltips (hover_x/hover_y), slot ids and accepted_backpack_items to identify input/output and controls. Prefer observed slot transfers or native widget/coordinate input, not invented machine-specific APIs. Native Forge play messages run through the maid's isolated connection; the owner's player/menu/inventory remain separate. After every operation check authoritative server slots, carried stack and actual maid inventory changes. A successful click, changing progress bar, or empty input is not proof of finished output. Use wait_gui with observed output_slot, exact item/count and owner wait policy, and complete only after verified delivery. If capture/protocol state is unavailable, report the actual reason; do not guess controls, completion or machine recipes.\n"
            + "At ProjectE transmutation tables use gui_action projecte_search(text or exact item,offset,limit), projecte_deposit(backpack_slot,count), and projecte_exchange(item,selection,count). Read adapter_state: the OWNER's live EMC and knowledge are shared, inputs/outputs use only the unlocked MAID backpack. Search returns learned variants including unaffordable ones and selection tokens for NBT variants. Do not use workbench recipes, native slot clicks or visual widgets for EMC exchange. Deposit only the items/quantities authorized by the owner; never burn unrelated backpack contents to fund a goal. Exchange count is exact NEW output for this call; read exchanged_count/emc_spent and subtract committed output before retries. Register transfer completion for requested output at the table; if a deposit is also required, include its outbound transfer in the full completion contract.\n"
            + "For workbench crafting, query_recipes once for the loaded pack recipe before choosing ingredients. If the owner's item name is fuzzy, speech-recognized or colloquial, pass that phrase as item: the tool resolves registered display names and returns resolved_item/item_candidates without guessing when several items match. Never web-search to identify a pack item name. Reuse Known crafting and cooking recipes after compression; query again only for missing recipes or recipe/tag reload. Open the workbench first, then use gui_action(action=fill_recipe,recipe_id) for one execution or gui_action(action=craft_recipe,recipe_id,count) for NEW products. These are action values, never standalone tools to load. Counts are per call, not total lifetime inventory. Read actual crafted_count/crafts_executed and subtract delivered products when retrying a partial result; native batches may produce explicitly reported surplus. Do not substitute remembered vanilla recipes for loaded mod/datapack recipes.\n"
            + "For exact owner-specified items, quantities and container coordinates, scan to verify positions, then register the FULL contract and open the first source in ONE response. Do not call inspect_containers to reconfirm those known amounts: open_gui supplies live slots before any transfer. Bulk inspection is for unknown/all quantities or unresolved allocation. Required restoration baselines and unfamiliar-machine inspection still apply.\n"
            + "Execute the next observed action or ordered batch. Once the FULL contract is registered, do not call update_task_plan merely to mark progress or list the next tools. Verified phases and receipts advance independently of the descriptive current_step; it may lag safely. Optionally put next_step on a real GUI action/opening to update its index after success, without resending the plan. Use one descriptive step per owner phase, grouping repeated container visits; do not advance next_step per container. Complete known operations in the same batch; wait for observations only when later arguments actually depend on the result.\n"
            + "Use completion.kind=sequence with a separate phase for EVERY owner-required intermediate milestone or opposing transfer leg. If the owner requires holding all products before delivery, put inventory(item,count) in its own phase BEFORE outbound transfers; manufacturing and delivery must not be merged. A phase can use all for simultaneous item requirements; each phase has its own NET transfer baseline and earlier phases retain verified receipts. Taking then returning items is NOT a final outbound net transfer. Include container_unchanged for original slot/count/NBT restoration (baseline requires the current open single container before mutations), and backpack_empty when requested. The final phase is checked against current facts. Ordinary single-leg transfer conditions still use final net amounts.\n"
            + "Match the owner's requested sources and number of containers. Scans may include unrelated neighbouring chests or repeated category labels; do not inspect or collect all candidates automatically. If multiple groups fit and the requested sources cannot be distinguished, ask the owner and pause rather than broadening the goal." + "\n"
            + "Tool schemas are selected automatically for the current observation, planning, execution or verification stage. Invoke tools present directly; do not load group:gui before normal container work. Combine initial/amended contract registration with an already known open_gui target in the SAME ordered response. With an open planning menu and observed slots, register completion BEFORE the first mutation in that SAME batch. Only unresolved arguments require another observation turn. Load only a registered capability missing for an owner requirement. A verification-stage menu does not declare the task completed or discard additional requirements." + "\n"
            + "Observe the current signs/containers and inventory, then call update_task_plan with completion covering EVERY requested item, quantity and source/destination. For 'take everything' with unknown amounts, use ONE inspect_containers(targets) call for all observed container positions; use its counts to define the full contract and operate the still-open active_gui first. If the owner already specified exact quantities/containers, register them without a separate inspection tour. GUI inspection is allowed; gui_action/gui_batch/wait_gui item mutations or collection are blocked until this condition is defined. Do not invent dummy conditions or assume success from a sentence." + "\n"
            + "Use these current server facts to check all explicit user requirements. A craft-only request ends with the required products in the MAID backpack; never invent owner delivery, player-menu opening or a separate inspection milestone. Explicitly requested delivery/arrival/restoration remains mandatory and needs its own completion evidence. On the FINAL gui_action/gui_batch that will satisfy ALL owner requirements, set complete_task=true: the tool performs actual actions, closes/settles the menu and requests runtime verification in this same call, with no final model report round. For intermediate transfers set close_after=true when done with that menu, and optionally put the next open_gui in the SAME ordered tool batch. Do not close a menu in a separate model turn. When completion cannot be declared with the last GUI action (e.g. additional arrival), call update_task_plan with complete=true at the last step after satisfying it. Do not reopen containers solely to reconfirm quantities or emptiness already covered by complete live source_checks. Unknown/unloaded/double-container coverage still requires observation. Verified predicates do not replace additional user requirements." + "\n"
            + "When recording a plan, set allowed_tools for a phase repeatedly using a stable small set with substantial schema savings; omit for short, mixed or uncertain phases. Repeated container visits are one phase, not isolated short tasks. Never inspect, load or send a planning-only request just to choose tools. Prefer next_allowed_tools on an already needed open_gui; active selections can also change inline on actions. It applies after success for the NEXT request. Include actual actions after preparation: [open_gui,gui_batch] for repeated transfers. Do not narrow a one-shot inventory/crafting milestone: ordinary execution schemas already include gui_action, and query_recipes alone cannot craft. The runtime can infer a stable native transfer loop from committed receipts without a selection-only request. Keep the same selection throughout a stable phase; do not rewrite it per container or menu close. Use close_after=true and put the next known open_gui in the SAME response. Step/owner/verified phase changes or recovery clear restrictions. Selection never changes owner requirements or receipts.\n";
}
